WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.379
"I am healed!" cried Katie. "I'm as good as new!"

2
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.884
Larry helped Katie into the hay wagon.

3
00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:23.808
Then he grabbed Joy's hand and pulled her up too.

4
00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:29.216
Larry's father, Mr. Ferguson, was sitting up front on his tractor.

5
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:33.267
"AJ, is everybody aboard?" he asked.

6
00:00:33.268 --> 00:00:37.872
AJ looked around at his friends sitting on bundles of hay.

7
00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:40.597
He looked up at his big sister Emily.

8
00:00:40.598 --> 00:00:42.997
She smiled and nodded.

9
00:00:42.998 --> 00:00:47.561
"All aboard, Mr. Ferguson!" shouted AJ.

10
00:00:47.562 --> 00:00:50.630
Mr. Ferguson started the tractor motor.

11
00:00:50.631 --> 00:00:53.900
The hayride had begun.

12
00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:58.483
"Happy Birthday to you," sang Laura.

13
00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:01.978
AJ put his hands over his face.

14
00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:08.070
"Happy Birthday to you," sang everybody.

15
00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:17.630
"Happy Birthday, dear AJ, Happy Birthday to you!"

16
00:01:17.631 --> 00:01:22.836
All the kids cheered and clapped.

17
00:01:22.837 --> 00:01:28.274
"How old are you?" asked Katie. "Four? Five?"

18
00:01:28.275 --> 00:01:34.252
AJ jumped up. "I'm six years old and you know it!" he said.

19
00:01:34.253 --> 00:01:37.072
Katie smiled and winked at him.

20
00:01:37.073 --> 00:01:42.427
Manny reached behind Laura and brushed her neck with a piece of straw.

21
00:01:42.428 --> 00:01:47.920
"Ooh!" cried Laura. "Something is crawling on me!"

22
00:01:47.921 --> 00:01:52.629
"A big, hairy spider!" said Luke.

23
00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:57.763
Laura screeched. "Get it off me!"

24
00:01:57.764 --> 00:02:02.797
"It's too big," said Luke. "I'm afraid to touch it!"

25
00:02:02.798 --> 00:02:06.264
Everybody laughed.

26
00:02:06.265 --> 00:02:11.271
"There's no spider," said Joy. "Luke, stop teasing."

27
00:02:11.272 --> 00:02:16.669
"Okay," said Luke. "There are no spiders on this wagon.

28
00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.355
And I hope there aren't any black snakes either!"

29
00:02:20.356 --> 00:02:23.199
Olivia punched Luke's arm.

30
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.565
"That was a very big black snake, and it wanted to bite me!"

31
00:02:28.566 --> 00:02:31.591
"That's not what I heard," said Larry.

32
00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:34.226
"I heard you scared it to death!"

33
00:02:34.227 --> 00:02:38.263
Everyone laughed again.

34
00:02:38.264 --> 00:02:41.241
"What a day that was," said Joy.

35
00:02:41.242 --> 00:02:43.996
"First, my helper got hurt.

36
00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:47.710
Then, the price of walnuts dropped—again!

37
00:02:47.711 --> 00:02:50.954
I thought I would never reach my goal."

38
00:02:50.955 --> 00:02:54.449
"What did you do?" asked AJ.

39
00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.753
"Well, I just kept picking walnuts," said Joy.

40
00:02:58.754 --> 00:03:04.115
"But Katie and Olivia called Luke, Larry, Laura, and Carlos.

41
00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:07.602
They all showed up on Sunday morning to help me."

42
00:03:07.603 --> 00:03:11.300
"Me too," said Manny.

43
00:03:11.301 --> 00:03:14.691
"Yes! You too," said Joy.

44
00:03:14.692 --> 00:03:20.412
"With so many people, we were able to fill the cart quickly," said Olivia.

45
00:03:20.413 --> 00:03:27.610
"Whenever the cart was full, Mr. Donovan and Joy took it to the nut-buying station," said Laura.

46
00:03:27.611 --> 00:03:31.374
"We filled the cart three times."

47
00:03:31.375 --> 00:03:35.081
"I did better than my goal," said Joy.

48
00:03:35.082 --> 00:03:41.584
"I earned one hundred eleven dollars and fifty-five cents!—thanks to my friends."

49
00:03:41.585 --> 00:03:45.137
"Is your fiddle fixed?" asked AJ.

50
00:03:45.138 --> 00:03:47.462
"It's in the shop," said Joy.

51
00:03:47.463 --> 00:03:50.195
"Soon it will be as good as new!"

52
00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:54.045
"Just like my ankle!" said Katie.

53
00:03:54.046 --> 00:03:59.803
The hay wagon bounced down the trail. Mr. Ferguson started a song.

54
00:03:59.804 --> 00:04:02.720
Old Dan Tucker was a mighty man.

55
00:04:02.721 --> 00:04:06.353
He washed his face in a frying pan.

56
00:04:06.354 --> 00:04:08.223
The kids joined in.

57
00:04:08.224 --> 00:04:11.463
Joy played an imaginary fiddle.

58
00:04:11.464 --> 00:04:14.226
He combed his hair with a wagon wheel.

59
00:04:14.227 --> 00:04:18.492
And died with a toothache in his heel.

60
00:04:18.493 --> 00:04:23.305
The kids sang, and Mr. Ferguson drove into the woods.

61
00:04:23.306 --> 00:04:27.779
They hadn't gone too far when Carlos saw something.

62
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.402
"It looks like a bonfire!" he said.

63
00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:35.022
"It is a bonfire," said Laura.

64
00:04:35.023 --> 00:04:38.724
"It's AJ's dad," cried Katie.

65
00:04:38.725 --> 00:04:44.326
"You're finally here," shouted Mr. Morgan, AJ and Emily's dad.

66
00:04:44.327 --> 00:04:48.319
"I thought I might have to roast the hot dogs all by myself."

67
00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.133
Everyone jumped out of the hay wagon.

68
00:04:52.134 --> 00:04:56.205
"Welcome to AJ's birthday bonfire!" said Emily.

69
00:04:56.206 --> 00:05:02.052
"Who wants hot apple cider?"

70
00:05:02.053 --> 00:05:06.657
"AJ has to make a birthday wish!" said Katie.

71
00:05:06.658 --> 00:05:10.278
"I can't tell you my birthday wish," said AJ.

72
00:05:10.279 --> 00:05:13.240
"Then it won't come true!"

73
00:05:13.241 --> 00:05:16.227
Joy smiled at the little boy.

74
00:05:16.228 --> 00:05:18.640
"Well, make another wish then.

75
00:05:18.641 --> 00:05:22.443
It doesn't have to be your birthday wish," she said.

76
00:05:22.444 --> 00:05:26.437
"And then you can tell us!" added Katie.

77
00:05:26.438 --> 00:05:29.513
"Okay," said AJ.

78
00:05:29.514 --> 00:05:36.411
"I wish to have the biggest birthday hayride in Willow Creek next year!

79
00:05:36.412 --> 00:05:41.821
I'll invite everyone!"
